### Removing columns with negative indexing

Use `dat[, -i.remove]` to drop specific columns. The comma separates **row** selection (left, empty = all rows) from **column** selection (right).

```{=html}
<div class="chunk-track" data-chunk-id="w2_c11">
```
```{shinylive-r}
#| standalone: true
#| viewerHeight: 270
library(shiny)
CHUNK_ID <- "w2_c11"
DAT <- data.frame(
  age    = c(46, 29, 58),
  chol   = c(203, 165, 228),
  bp.2s  = c(NA, NA, NA),
  time.ppn = c(NA, NA, NA)
)
ui <- fluidPage(
  tags$script('Shiny.addCustomMessageHandler("chunkRun",function(m){window.parent.postMessage({type:"chunkDone",chunkId:m.chunkId},"*");});'),
  textAreaInput("code", "Remove columns", value = "# Find indices of columns to remove\ni.remove <- which(colnames(dat) %in% c('bp.2s', 'time.ppn'))\ni.remove\n\n# Remove them (negative index = exclude)\ndat.clean <- dat[, -i.remove]\ndat.clean", width = '100%', height = '110px'),
  actionButton("run", "Run Code", class = "btn-success"),
  verbatimTextOutput("out")
)
server <- function(input, output, session) {
